---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe35.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Identifying Operating Segments — the Management Approach" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Chief Operating Decision Maker" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Quantitative Thresholds for Reportable Segments" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Aggregation of Similar Segments" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Reconciliations to Consolidated Totals" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Applying the 10% Revenue Threshold" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Reconciling Segment Profit to Consolidated Profit" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IFRS 8" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Reporting through the eyes of management</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 35 governs the IDENTIFICATION and DISCLOSURE of OPERATING SEGMENTS — COMPONENTS of an ENTERPRISE that ENGAGE in BUSINESS activities from WHICH it MAY earn REVENUES and INCUR expenses, and WHOSE operating RESULTS are REGULARLY reviewed by the ENTITY'S chief OPERATING decision MAKER. THE Standard APPLIES the SAME "MANAGEMENT approach" as IFRS 8 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Listed companies with distinguishable business components</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to LISTED companies (and OTHERS choosing to DISCLOSE segment INFORMATION), REQUIRING disclosure of INFORMATION enabling USERS to EVALUATE the NATURE and financial EFFECTS of the BUSINESS activities the ENTERPRISE engages IN, and the ECONOMIC environments it OPERATES within.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Identifying Operating Segments — the Management Approach</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Based on internal reporting structure, not externally imposed categories</div><div class="text-supporting">OPERATING segments are IDENTIFIED based on the ENTERPRISE'S OWN INTERNAL organisational and REPORTING structure — HOW management ITSELF views and MANAGES the BUSINESS INTERNALLY — RATHER than an EXTERNALLY imposed INDUSTRY or GEOGRAPHIC classification SCHEME.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Chief Operating Decision Maker</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The function allocating resources and assessing performance</div><div class="text-supporting">The "CHIEF OPERATING DECISION MAKER" is a FUNCTION (NOT necessarily a SINGLE individual) RESPONSIBLE for ALLOCATING resources TO, and ASSESSING the PERFORMANCE of, an ENTERPRISE'S operating SEGMENTS — the INFORMATION THIS function REGULARLY reviews FORMS the BASIS for IDENTIFYING segments.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Quantitative Thresholds for Reportable Segments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Any single 10% test qualifies a segment for separate reporting</div><div class="text-supporting">AN operating SEGMENT is a REPORTABLE segment WHERE its REVENUE, PROFIT or LOSS, or ASSETS represent 10% OR more of the COMBINED totals for ALL operating SEGMENTS — MEETING ANY ONE of these THREE tests QUALIFIES a segment for SEPARATE disclosure.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Aggregation of Similar Segments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Combining segments with similar economic characteristics</div><div class="text-supporting">TWO or MORE operating SEGMENTS with SIMILAR economic CHARACTERISTICS (SIMILAR products, PRODUCTION processes, CUSTOMER types, and REGULATORY environments) MAY be AGGREGATED into a SINGLE reportable SEGMENT, WHERE aggregation is CONSISTENT with this Standard'S core PRINCIPLES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Reconciliations to Consolidated Totals</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Bridging segment totals to the consolidated financial statements</div><div class="text-supporting">TOTAL segment REVENUE, profit or LOSS, and ASSETS must be RECONCILED to the ENTERPRISE'S CONSOLIDATED totals — ENSURING readers CAN trace SEGMENT-level information BACK to the OVERALL, CONSOLIDATED financial STATEMENTS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying the 10% Revenue Threshold</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Determining which segments qualify for separate reporting</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A diversified group with four business lines</div><div class="wk-body">A group's combined segment revenue across four business lines totals RMB 1,000,000,000. Segment A generates RMB 350,000,000; Segment B, RMB 90,000,000; Segment C, RMB 460,000,000; Segment D, RMB 100,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The 10% THRESHOLD is RMB 100,000,000. SEGMENTS A (RMB 350,000,000), C (RMB 460,000,000), and D (RMB 100,000,000) MEET the THRESHOLD and are REPORTABLE SEPARATELY; SEGMENT B (RMB 90,000,000) does NOT meet the REVENUE test ALONE, though it MAY still QUALIFY if it MEETS the PROFIT or ASSETS threshold INSTEAD.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Reconciling Segment Profit to Consolidated Profit</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Bridging segment totals with unallocated corporate items</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Unallocated corporate expenses</div><div class="wk-body">A company's total reportable segment profit sums to RMB 200,000,000, but the group's consolidated profit before tax is RMB 175,000,000, due to RMB 25,000,000 of unallocated corporate overhead not attributed to any segment.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company DISCLOSES a RECONCILIATION: total SEGMENT profit RMB 200,000,000 LESS unallocated CORPORATE expenses RMB 25,000,000 = CONSOLIDATED profit before TAX of <strong>RMB 175,000,000</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 35 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Factors used to identify reportable segments, and the basis of organisation</span><span>Segment revenue, profit or loss, assets, and liabilities</span><span>Reconciliations of segment totals to consolidated financial statement totals</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Identifying the chief operating decision maker and the segments it reviews</span><span>Whether operating segments with similar characteristics should be aggregated</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Allocation basis for shared costs and assets across segments</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 8</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 35 vs IFRS 8</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 35</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 8</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Management approach</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>10% quantitative thresholds</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, MIRRORING IFRS 8'S management APPROACH closely.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every segment disclosure lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Segment disclosures</span><span>Notes only</span><span>No effect on the primary financial statement figures</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 33</span><span>Consolidated Financial Statements — supplies the consolidated totals this Standard's reconciliations tie back to</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Operating segment</div><div class="glossary-def">A component of an enterprise engaging in business activities, whose results are regularly reviewed by the chief operating decision maker.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Chief operating decision maker</div><div class="glossary-def">The function responsible for allocating resources to, and assessing the performance of, an enterprise's operating segments.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe35 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
